        "Now we face the futurist's strongest prooftext head-on: 1 Thessalonians 4:16-17. 'For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Christ shall rise first: Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord.'\n\nFuturists seize upon 'caught up' (Greek: harpazo, Latin: rapturo — from which 'rapture' derives) and 'meet the Lord in the air' to argue for a snatching away of believers before the tribulation. We must give this argument its full weight before dismantling it.\n\nThe futurist reads this passage as: believers are secretly removed from earth, taken to heaven, while the world continues into tribulation. The historicist/Adventist reads the same passage as describing the second coming: a visible, audible, glorious event where both resurrected and living saints ascend to meet the returning Christ.",
