      jeevesDebrief:
        "Precise logical analysis, soldier. The appeal to fear is the most common fallacy in rapture evangelism. It converts more people than exegesis ever has — not because the evidence supports the rapture but because the fear of being wrong is paralyzing. Your task is to break the fear cycle by showing that truth is determined by Scripture, not by anxiety. When someone says, 'What if you are wrong?' the calm response is: 'Let us look at what the Bible actually says about Christ's return and let the evidence guide us.'",
